<title>JAPAN: Toray plans polyester output in Czech Rep -- paper.</title>
<headline>Toray plans polyester output in Czech Rep -- paper.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Toray Industries Inc will invest an estimated 10 billion yen to start producing polyester fibre in the Czech Republic from as early as 1999, a Japanese business daily said on Monday.</p>
<p>The Nihon Keizai Shimbun said Toray would be the first Japanese synthetic fibre maker to produce in eastern Europe.</p>
<p>The size and details of the planned polyester output had not yet been decided, the paper said.</p>
<p>Toray was not immediately available for comment.</p>
</text>
